    "q-105542": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105542",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elimination. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,-6,$ and $-7.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
