    "q-32810": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32810",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 20 & 40 & -15\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$",
      "worked_solution": "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 20 & 40 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-4)=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
