    "q-107161": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107161",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $B=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $B$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{43}\\cdot {u}_{24}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $B$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & \\,2\\, & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & \\,2\\, & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{43}=-4$ and ${u}_{24}=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{43}\\cdot {u}_{24}=(-4)\\cdot (-6)=24.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
